cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use this app in research, cite Supraspina as specified below and credit the pinned upstream SCI_Map project for methods or assets used in the work (see references). The license field covers first-party code only, as scoped in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES; bundled and acquired third-party material keeps its own terms, recorded there and in THIRD_PARTY_PROVENANCE.json.'
type: software
title: 'Supraspina'
version: '20261122.2152.0'
date-released: '2026-11-22'
doi: '10.5281/zenodo.24451026'
abstract: 'Supraspina is a Linux Electron research console for a 14-stage structural-MRI workflow. It drives SynthStrip, FreeSurfer recon-all or FastSurfer, ENIGMA QC, PyBrainAge inference, BrainCharts normative modeling, and Rscript through supervised subprocesses; manages durable workflow scheduling, provenance, recovery, and process-tree cancellation; and presents cohort status, QC, results, and project configuration for review. Pipeline glue and downstream analysis stages use explicitly inventoried first-party implementations. The repository also includes the analysis code of a paper in analyses/. Supraspina is not a medical device or clinical decision system.'
authors:
  - given-names: 'Yusuf'
    family-names: 'Qwareeq'
    email: 'yusuf@qwareeq.com'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/qwareeq8/supraspina'
url: 'https://qwareeq.com/'
license: MIT
references:
